## Bandit Level 8 → Level 9


**Challenge:** 

The password for the next level is stored in the file data.txt and is the only line of text that occurs only once

Commands you may need to solve this level
grep, sort, uniq, strings, base64, tr, tar, gzip, bzip2, xxd


**Solution & Explanation:****
```
STEP 1: ls
# quick check of what’s in the current home directory
# data.txt is the only apparent file 

STEP 2: cat data.txt
# displayed a lot of lines of computer data

STEP 3: wc -l data.txt
# file has 1001 lines in it and we are only interested in one unique line with no duplicates
# rest of the lines have duplicates

STEP 4: sort data.txt
# this command will group identical lines of text in an alphabetized manner
# still difficult to find unique text

STEP 5: sort data.txt | uniq -u
# output of first command will be used by uniq command as an argument 
with the -u option that will show only unique (non-repeated) lines

```
**Password:** [4CKMh1JI91bUIZZPXDqGanal4xvAg0JM]


**USEFUL SINGLE COMMAND LINE**

sort data.txt | uniq -u


**What I learned:** 

uniq only works correctly on sorted input

sort → groups identical lines together

uniq -u → shows only unique (non-repeated) lines

| (pipe) → sends output of one command into the next

👉 Mental model: organize first, then filter
